course: dictionary
lesson: 10335
title: Traitor: letting people down
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A traitor is someone who lets down people who trusted them. They might help the enemies of their country, or they might give away a friend's secret or switch sides in a team or group. Because it is a strong word, it is worth knowing exactly what it means.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «When he opens his eyes, his own river looks grey and chilly, and his loyal heart scolds him for being a traitor.» The word loyal is the clue here. A loyal heart stays true, so a traitor is someone who does not stay true.
explain: Playground talk uses the word too. «Jake lives on Station Road but goes to school with the Mill Lane kids, so both sides called him a traitor.» Jake did not betray a country. Both groups felt he had let them down by mixing with the other side. To check, swap in your meaning: "both sides felt let down by him" still makes sense.
fact: Traitor is a noun: one traitor, many traitors.
fact: «Traitor» means a person who betrays their country, or who betrays friends, a team or a group by giving away secrets or changing sides.
fact: «Loyal» is the opposite of traitor: a loyal person stays true to their friends and their country.
fact: «Turn traitor» means to suddenly become a traitor.
fact: «You traitor!» is often shouted half as a joke in the playground, but the word can still hurt.
exercise: «Jake lives on Station Road but goes to school with the Mill Lane kids, so both sides called him a traitor.» Why did both sides call Jake a traitor? | He had moved to a new country | He had won a race for his school | He had lost his lunch | *He had let both sides down by mixing with the other one
exercise: What does a traitor do? | *Betrays people or their country by giving away secrets or changing sides | Keeps a friend's secret safe | Wins every game for the team
exercise: Sam's «friend» says «only joking», then sends cruel messages. The message says «if u block me ur a snake». In this story, what animal is used to mean a traitor? | Rabbit | Owl | Fox | *Snake
test: «Turn traitor» means | Winning a prize for being kind | Going to a new school | *Suddenly becoming a traitor by changing sides
test: Which sentence uses traitor correctly? | *The soldier was called a traitor because he gave his country's secrets to its enemies | She was a traitor because she sang loudly in the choir | The sun was a traitor, shining all day long
exam: Which word in «his loyal heart scolds him for being a traitor» is the opposite of traitor? | *Loyal | Heart | Scolds | River
